          {
            "typeName": "notesText",
            "multiple": false,
            "typeClass": "primitive",
            "value": "Method: Interpretative Phenomenological Analysis was applied to investigate the lived experiences with respect to self-determination of people with mild intellectual disabilities and drug resistant epilepsy. We used semi-structured interviews to collect the data. <br>Data analysis consisted of the following stages:<br>\n1. Analysis of each separate interview on descriptive, linguisticand conceptual level and formulation <br>\n2. Identification of emergent themes of each interview <br>\n3. Clustering and formulation of themes and interconnectedsubthemes of each interview <br>\n4. Comparison of themes and narratives across interviews<br><br>\nUniverse: The group of people were adult men and women with a mild to borderline intellectual disability and drug-resistant epilepsy from the Netherlands. <br><br>\nEthical approval was provided by the Ethics Review Board of Tilburg University (RP305))."
          },
